(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence"
An **event_occurrence** is the fact of a transition between states at some point in time. The description of the **event_occurrrnece** can provide an implicit representation of either the state preceeding the **event_occurrence** or the state after the **event_occurrence**.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence.__example"
The *event_occurrence* 'start of production' implicitly declares that the before the *event_occurrence* a product was not in production.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence.__note"
The point in time of the existence may not be known in terms of a calendar date before the *event_occurrence* actually happens. One reason, why the *event_occurrence* cannot always be expressed as a calendar date, is that the *event_occurrence* is not possible to plan, for example a break down of a machine.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **event_occurrence**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **event_occurrence**.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **event_occurrence** is known.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence_context_role"
An **event_occurrence_context_role** establishes a context for an <<express:management_resources_schema.event_occurrence_assignment,event_occurrence_assignment>>. An **event_occurrence** is an incompletely modeled concept and requires population of related entity data types for formation of a complete instance of **event_occurrence_context_role**
*)

(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence_context_role.__example"
For the <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence,event_occurrence>> 'start of production' the product, for which production starts, is the context for that <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence,event_occurrence>>.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence_context_role.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **event_occurrence_context_role**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence_context_role.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **event_occurrence_context_role** is known.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.event_occurrence_relationship"
An **event_occurrence_relationship** is a relationship between two <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence,event_occurrence>>s with a description of their relationship.
*)


