(*"date_time_schema.local_time"
A **local_time** is an instance of time represented on a 24-hour clock by hour, minute, and second. The instance is expressed in the local time zone and the offset with the coordinate universal time shall be specified. This concept is defined in ISO 8601.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.local_time.__note"
This construct is used to represent a moment of time whereas <<express:measure_schema.time_measure,time_measure>> represents amounts of time.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.local_time.hour_component"
the number of hours.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.local_time.minute_component"
the number of minutes. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.local_time.second_component"
the number of seconds. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.local_time.zone"
the offset of the local time zone to the coordinated universal time.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.local_time.wr:WR1"
The entity shall define a valid time. The **second_component** attribute shall only exist if the **minute_component** attribute exists.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.ordinal_date"
An **ordinal_date** is a type of <<express:date_time_schema.date,date>> defined as a day of a year. This concept is defined in ISO 8601.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.ordinal_date.day_component"
the day element of the <<express:date_time_schema.date,date>>.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.ordinal_date.wr:WR1"
The **day_component** shall be between 1 and 365 if the <<express:date_time_schema.date.year_component,year_component>> is not a leap year. Otherwise the **day_component** shall be between 1 and 366.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.relative_event_occurrence"
A **relative_event_occurrence** is a type of <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence,event_occurrence>> that takes place with an offset to an <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence,event_occurrence>>.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.relative_event_occurrence.__example"
'Five days after start of production' is an example for a *relative_event_occurrence*, where 'five days' is an offset relative to an <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence,event_occurrence>> 'start of production'.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.relative_event_occurrence.base_event"
the **relative_event_occurrence** is defined with respect to the **base_event**.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.relative_event_occurrence.offset"
the amount of time that passes between the occurrence of the **base_event** and the **relative_event_occurrence**. A negative offset specifies that the **relative_event_occurrence** occurs before the **base_event**.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.time_interval"
A **time_interval** is the identification of an interval of time. This concept is defined in ISO 8601.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.time_interval.__example"
'Strike duration', 'delay of production', and 'Christmas holidays' are examples for **time_interval**s.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.time_interval.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **time_interval**.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.time_interval.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.time_interval.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **time_interval** is known.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.time_interval.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **time_interval**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.time_interval_relationship"
A **time_interval_relationship** is a relationship between two <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval,time_interval>>s with a description of their relationship.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.time_interval_relationship.__note"
The role of *time_interval_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.time_interval_relationship.__note"
This entity, together with the <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval,time_interval>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3.
*)

