*)

(*"date_time_schema.week_of_year_and_day_date"
A **week_of_year_and_day_date** is a type of <<express:date_time_schema.date,date>> defined by identifying the week within a year and the day within that particular week.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.week_of_year_and_day_date.day_component"
the day element of the <<express:date_time_schema.date,date>>.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.week_of_year_and_day_date.week_component"
the week element of the <<express:date_time_schema.date,date>>.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.week_of_year_and_day_date.wr:WR1"
The result of the expression **day_component** + (7 * <<express:date_time_schema.week_of_year_and_day_date.week_component,week_component>>) shall be between 1 and 366 if the <<express:date_time_schema.date.year_component,year_component>> is a leap year.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.week_of_year_and_day_date.wr:WR2"
The result of the expression **day_component** + (7 * <<express:date_time_schema.week_of_year_and_day_date.week_component,week_component>>) shall be between 1 and 365 if the <<express:date_time_schema.date.year_component,year_component>> is not a leap year.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.year_month"
A **year_month** is a type of <<express:date_time_schema.date,date>> defined as a month of a year.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.year_month.month_component"
the month element of the <<express:date_time_schema.date,date>>.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_event_occurrence_relationship"
The **acyclic_event_occurrence_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence,event_occurrence>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence_relationship,event_occurrence_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_event_occurrence_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_event_occurrence_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence_relationship,event_occurrence_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_event_occurrence_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence_relationship,event_occurrence_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_event_occurrence_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence,event_occurrence>> for which the function is searching in the <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence_relationship.relating_event,relating_event>> parameter of the relation argument.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_event_occurrence_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified entity name of a type of <<express:date_time_schema.event_occurrence_relationship,event_occurrence_relationship>> entity.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_time_interval_relationship"
The **acyclic_time_interval_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval,time_interval>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either a <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_relationship,time_interval_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_time_interval_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_time_interval_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_relationship,time_interval_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_time_interval_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_relationship,time_interval_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_time_interval_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval,time_interval>> for which the function is searching in the <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_relationship.relating_time_interval,relating_time_interval>> parameter of the relation argument.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.acyclic_time_interval_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified entity name of a type of <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_relationship,time_interval_relationship>> entity.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.duration_is_negative"
The **duration_is_negative** function determines whether a given <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_with_bounds.duration,duration>> is negative. It returns TRUE if the <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_with_bounds.duration,duration>> is negative. Otherwise, it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.duration_is_negative.duration"
(input) the candidate <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_with_bounds.duration,duration>> that is being checked.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.duration_is_positive"
The **duration_is_positive** function determines whether a given <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_with_bounds.duration,duration>> is positive. It returns TRUE if the <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_with_bounds.duration,duration>> is a positive. Otherwise, it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.duration_is_positive.duration"
(input) the candidate <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_with_bounds.duration,duration>> that is being checked.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.leap_year"
The **leap_year** function checks whether or not a particular year contains 366 days instead of 365 days, known as a leap year.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.leap_year.__note"
Leap years occur every for years.
*)

(*"date_time_schema.leap_year.year"
an integer representing a particular year in the Gregorian calendar.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.valid_calendar_date"
The **valid_calendar_date** function determines whether the components of a <<express:date_time_schema.calendar_date,calendar_date>> indicate a valid <<express:date_time_schema.date,date>>. If the <<express:date_time_schema.calendar_date,calendar_date>> is valid, the function returns TRUE. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.valid_calendar_date.date"
(input) the candidate <<express:date_time_schema.calendar_date,calendar_date>> that is to be checked.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.valid_time"
The **valid_time** function determines whether a candidate <<express:date_time_schema.local_time,local_time>> has a <<express:date_time_schema.local_time.minute_component,minute_component>> if it has a <<express:date_time_schema.local_time.second_component,second_component>>. It returns FALSE if the condition is not met. Otherwise it returns TRUE.
*)


(*"date_time_schema.valid_time.time"
(input) the candidate <<express:date_time_schema.local_time,local_time>> that is to be checked.
*)


